        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "processQuery"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770811004538"
          },
          "code": "PROCESSQUERY",
          "id": "1770810818766",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770810818767_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Inputs\n\n- `history`: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n- `userQuery`: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- `attachmentData`: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAttachments}}\n\n### Goal\n\nReturn only the relevant context for the same issue, detect intent, build a framedQuery.\n\n### Rules\n\n## 1. Context Extraction\n\n- Add details from `attachmentData` to `context` relevant to `userQuery`.\n- Review `history` in order.\n  - `userQuery` has priority over `attachmentData`.\n  - Add prior user turns verbatim if they match the topic of `userQuery` and `attachmentData`(same issue, clarification, or resolution—not a completely different request).\n  - Extract only prior AI turns that are a direct response to relevant user turns about the same topic as `userQuery` and `attachmentData`, and convert them to neutral third-person facts (e.g., “System checked and found no payslips available”).\n  - Do not include prior AI answers or confirmations about unrelated tickets, status, or actions. \n  - Ignore all other `history`: unrelated user requests, AI confirmations, unrelated ticket logs or unrelated queries, greetings, and non-actionable exchanges.\n  - If the preceding user turns contain a vague ticket request (e.g., “log a ticket”) and there has been no successful ticket confirmation or explicit user cancellation/decline since, append that ticket request.\n  - If there are multiple unresolved issues that are not related in `history`, pick up the most recent issue.\n  - Exclude salutations, system confirmations or suggested next steps.\n  - Do not include multiple unrelated issues.\n  - Set this as `context`.\n- If `isReport` is true, set `context` as \"\" **(empty string)**.\n\n\n## 2. Intent Detection\n\nClassify the intent into **exactly one** category from `context`, `userQuery` and `attachmentData`:\n\n1. **logTicket**\n   - User explicitly mentions logging, raising, creating a ticket/SR. `intent` is **not** logTicket if in `history`, the user requested ticket logging and ticket has been logged successfully (in this order). `intent` is \"logTicket\" **until and unless** ticket has been logged successfully or the user explicitly says not to log a ticket.\n2. **srReport**\n   - User requests information about SRs/tickets such as list, status, summary, or details.\n   - Includes any query referring to a **specific existing SR/ticket/issue record**, even if phrased briefly or without explicit keywords like \"status\" or \"details\".\n3. **salutation**\n   - `userQuery` contains only a greeting, courtesy phrase, basic engagement phrase (such as \"how can you help?\", \"what can you do?\", \"how do you work?\", \"who are you?\", etc) or high-level orientation question about you (\"how do i use Ask Oracle?\").\n4. **learnings**\n   - Reference to learnings. (e.g., learnings, trainings, courses, etc)\n5. **journeys**\n   - Reference to journeys.\n6. **absences**\n   - Reference to absences (e.g., vacation, PTO, sick leave, vacation balances).\n7. **query**\n   - All **informational, explanatory, advisory, or how-to questions**.\n   - This is the **default** category.\n8. Multiple intents\n   - If there are multiple intents in userQuery or you are unable to pick a single intent, set it as a list to `intent`. \n   - If userQuery clearly refers to the user's own records in one of these domains: absences, learnings, journeys AND userQuery is asking for help/troubleshooting/how-to (not just requesting the record), then set intent as a list: [<domainIntent>, \"query\"].\n   - Valid values for list containing **multiple** values: \"learnings\", \"journeys\", \"absences\", \"query\"\n\n- Valid values: \"logTicket\", \"srReport\", \"salutation\", \"learnings\", \"journeys\", \"absences\", \"query\"\n- **Topic ≠ intent**. Do not classify based on topic alone.\n- If the query is **general or informational**, include **query**.\n- Only include **absences / learnings / journeys** when there is a **clear reference to the user’s own records**.\n- When intent is unclear, choose **query**.\n\n## 3. Framed Query\n\n- If `intent` is \"salutation\"(hard override)\n  - `framedQuery` = `userQuery`\n  - No `context`, no combining, no rewriting.\n  - Do not include HTML, tables, SR lists, or metadata in `framedQuery`.\n- If `isReport` is false\n  - If `context` exists:\n    - framedQuery = \"<`context`>. User: <`userQuery`>\"\n  - Else:\n    - framedQuery = `userQuery`\n- Do not modify, rewrite, or extend `userQuery` in any way.\n- Do **not** prefix with \"User mentioned\" or \"Earlier said.\"  \n- Keep it concise and natural, e.g.,  \n  - ✅ \"payslip for September 2025 seems missing, log a ticket.\"  \n  - ❌ \"User mentioned missing payslip for September 2025, please log a ticket.\"  \n\n\n### Output (RFC8259 JSON)\n{\n  \"intent\": [],\n  \"framedQuery\": \"\",\n}\n\n---\n### **Examples**\n\n**Example 1:**  \nHistory: **User: My payslip for September 2025 is missing. AI:I couldn't find any payslips in your account. isReport=false**\n\nQuery: **Please log a ticket for that.**\n\n→  \n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": [\"logTicket\"],\n  \"framedQuery\": \"My payslip for September 2025 is missing. System indicated that no payslips were found. Please log a ticket for that.\"\n}\n```\n\n**Example 2:**  \nHistory: **empty**\n\nQuery: **Show my open SRs.**\n→  \n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": [\"srReport\"],\n  \"framedQuery\": \"Show my open SRs.\"\n}\n```\n**Example 3:**  \nHistory: **User: My payslip for September 2025 is missing. Log a ticket. AI: Ticket has been logged successfully. isReport=false**  \nQuery: **My payslip is missing for June 2025**  \n→  \n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": [\"query\"],\n  \"framedQuery\": \"A ticket was logged successfully for the earlier September 2025 payslip issue. My payslip is missing for June 2025.\"\n}\n```\n**Example 4:**  \nHistory: **empty**  \nQuery: **log a ticket.**  \n→  \n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": [\"logTicket\"],\n  \"framedQuery\": \"log a ticket.\"\n}\n```\n```json\n**Example 5:**  \nHistory: **User: My payslip for September 2025 is missing. Log a ticket. AI: Ticket has been logged successfully. isReport=false**  \nQuery: **Great, thanks!**  \n→  \n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": [\"salutation\"],\n  \"framedQuery\": \"great, thanks!\"\n}\n```\n```json\n**Example 6:**  \nHistory: \"\"\nQuery: **List my journeys and learnings**  \n→  \n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": [\"learnings\", \"journeys\"],\n  \"framedQuery\": \"List my journeys and learnings\"\n}\n```"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"framedQuery\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"intent\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8760,
            "y": 5428
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "getIntent",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const intent = $context.$nodes.PROCESSQUERY.$output.intent;\nlet newIntent = intent;\n\nif (intent.includes(\"logTicket\")) {\n  newIntent = [\"srReport\"];\n}\n\nreturn newIntent;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770811128252"
          },
          "code": "GETINTENT",
          "id": "1770811004538",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8760,
            "y": 5650
          }
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate final response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_FINAL_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1770811063863",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770811063864_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## ROLE\nYou are a **Helpdesk Virtual Agent**.\n\n## INPUT DATA\n- `queryOutput`: {{$context.$variables.queryOutput}}\n- `learningsOutput`: {{$context.$variables.learningsOutput}}\n- `journeysOutput`: {{$context.$variables.journeysOutput}}\n- `absencesOutput`: {{$context.$variables.absencesOutput}}\n- `existingSrsOutput`: {{$context.$variables.existingSrsOutput}}\n- `chatHistory`: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n## User Query\n- `userQuery`: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESSQUERY.$output.framedQuery}}\n\n## CAPABILITIES\n- Answer user questions using **only input data**.\n- Return output if {{$context.$variables.ticketLogged}} is true.\n- You can offer to log, create, or submit tickets, **only if** a ticket does not exist for the same exact issue mentioned in userQuery.\n\n## UI RULE\n- A **“Log a Ticket”** button **may be present** in the UI.\n- Do **NOT** mention or suggest logging a ticket unless explicitly required by the rules below.\n\n---\n\n## REQUIRED DECISION FLOW (CHOOSE EXACTLY ONE)\n\n### Case 1 — TICKET IS LOGGED\nIf {{$context.$variables.ticketLogged}} is true, return exactly `queryOutput` as response\n\n### Case 2 — OUT OF SCOPE\nIf the user asks you to **perform an action** you cannot do (submit requests, troubleshoot, change systems, etc.), respond **exactly**:\n\n> That is out of my scope. I can only answer using available data or log a help desk request.\n\n---\n\n### Case 3 — NO DATA FOUND\n- If the question is valid but input data does not explicitly support an answer, try to answer it **using the available data**. If still not possible, mention that.\n- If `existingSrsOutput` contains SRs for the **exact same issue**, append on a new line:\n  > For reference, the following SR(s) have already been logged for the same issue: <SR_NUMBER_1>, <SR_NUMBER_2>\n- Offer to create a service request for the query.\n- **Do not offer** to do anything outside of your capabilities.\n\n---\n\n### Case 4 — ANSWER FOUND\nIf input data explicitly supports the answer:\n\n1. Respond in a clear and concise format. Use a single paragraph by default. If the information naturally contains multiple distinct items (e.g., steps, options, conditions, or features), present them as a short, clean list instead.\n2. If `existingSrsOutput` contains SRs for the **exact same issue**, append on a new line:\n  > For reference, the following SR(s) have already been logged for the same issue: <SR_NUMBER_1>, <SR_NUMBER_2>\n3. Ensure that the output is **not repetitive** and is grammatically correct.\n4. **Do not offer** to do anything outside of your capabilities.\n\n---\n\n## ACTIONABLE INSIGHT RULE (CRITICAL)\n\nAdd a actionable insight with title \"Log a Ticket\" with action: ora.Agent({\"action\":\"logTicket\", \"issue\": \"<{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAttachments}}>\", \"queryOutput\":<your response here>}) **ONLY IF ALL are true**:\n- The user query describes an **issue/problem**\n- **AND** there are **no existing SRs** for that issue in `queryOutput`\n- **AND** if {{$context.$variables.ticketLogged}} is false\n\n### DO NOT add the actionable insight when:\n- The query is **informational** (e.g., “how to check engine oil level”)\n- The query is **not an issue**\n- Existing SRs already exist for the issue\n- If {{$context.$variables.ticketLogged}} is true\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT)\n- Output **ONLY** the final response text\n- No headings, labels, explanations, HTML, links, or tool syntax\n- If no actionable insight applies, **return only the response text**\n- Must Generate the output in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} language."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 9435,
            "y": 14026
          }
        },
