            "success": "1770821129732"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1770821085895",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770821085896_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Inputs\n- `ticketData`: {{$context.$nodes.GETSUMMARYISRREQUESTS.$output}} || {{$context.$nodes.GETSUMMARYHRREQUESTS.$output}}\n\n### Task\nYou are an **AI summarizing the ticket**. Generate a **single fluent summary under 100 words** based strictly on the provided ticket data.\n\n### Perspective Rules\n- Treat the **user as the customer**.\n- Refer to the customer as **“you”**.\n- Do **not** write as the customer or as a participant in the ticket.\n- Maintain a **neutral, third-person summarizer tone**.\n\n### Content Rules\n- Seamlessly incorporate:\n  - Ticket issue/description  \n  - Latest messageContent from messages\n  - Response status  \n  - Last updated date  \n  - Severity  \n  - Assignee status\n- Keep the narrative factual and chronological.\n- If {{$context.$nodes.PROCESSQUERY.$output.framedQuery}} asks for something more other than summary, include those details too if available in `ticketData`.\n\n### Message Interpretation Rules\n- If the latest message type is `ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY`, describe it as **something you said** (eg: “you asked…”, “you requested…”).\n- If the latest message type is `ORA_SVC_RESPONSE` or `ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE`, describe it as **something the agent said** (eg: “The agent asked…”, “Agent requested…”).\n- Do not imply progress, investigation, or action unless explicitly present.\n\n\n### Assignee Handling\n- If an assignee exists, mention them naturally.\n- If no assignee exists, explicitly state that **the ticket is currently unassigned**.\n\n### Constraints\n- Do not invent, or infer facts.\n- Do not include links.\n- Output **only the summary text**, nothing else.\n\n### OUTPUT_FORMAT (STRICT)\n- Must Generate the output in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} language."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8310,
            "y": 13138
          }
