        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "findSRRoute"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770812790542"
          },
          "code": "FINDSRROUTE",
          "id": "1770811285847",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770811285848_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##INPUT_SOURCE\n- `query`: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESSQUERY.$output.intent[0] == \"srReport\" ? $context.$system.$inputMessage : \"my open SRs\"}}\n\n### Routing Instructions\n\nYou are given a user `query`.  \nYour task is to determine the appropriate `route` and `keyword`.\n\n---\n\n#### Routing Rules\n\n1. **Open SRs**\n   - If the query asks to view the user’s open or active service requests  \n     (e.g., \"open SRs\", \"my SRs\", \"my open tickets\")  \n   - `route = \"open\"`  \n   - `keyword = \"\"`\n\n2. **Resolved SRs**\n   - If the query asks for resolved or closed service requests  \n     (e.g., \"resolved SRs\", \"closed tickets\")  \n   - `route = \"resolved\"`  \n   - `keyword = \"\"`\n\n3. **Summarize a Specific SR**\n   - If the query asks to summarize a specific SR and includes an SR number  \n   - `route = \"summary\"`  \n   - `keyword = <SR number from query>`\n\n4. **Issue-based Filter**\n   - Use this route **only when the query refers to a functional problem or topic**\n   - Examples:\n     - \"issues related to payslip\"\n     - \"tickets related to employment letter\"\n     - \"SRs about leave portal\"\n   - Do **not** treat attributes (eg: severity, priority, status, SLA, or time-based filters) as issues  \n   - `route = \"issue\"`  \n   - `keyword = <problem or topic extracted from query>`\n\n5. **Default**\n   - If the query filters by severity, priority, urgency, SLA, time, or other attributes  \n     (e.g., \"high severity tickets\", \"urgent SRs\", \"tickets raised last week\")\n   - Or if the query does not clearly match any rule above  \n   - `route = \"default\"`  \n   - `keyword = \"\"`"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"keyword\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"route\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6655,
            "y": 7036
          }
        },
